    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d415">

                <pb facs="0418" n="406" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg406"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.51A/1140: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Chargé in Iran</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Ford</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-05-25T14:00:00-04:00">May 25, 1944—2
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>325. Your 351, May 19. The note given in Department’s 303, May 17 is designed as
                    a preventative measure to forestall a crisis rather than to meet one which may
                    arise. Furthermore, the events which have already occurred fully justify
                    representations to the Iranian Government. Unless you perceive strong
                    objections, you should take an early occasion to deliver the note.</p>
                <p>As regards Dr. Millspaugh’s requested amendment, the Legation is on strong
                    grounds when making representations on the general subject of the advisory
                    program but should hesitate to press the <pb facs="0419" n="407" xml:id="pg407"
                    /> Iranians on specific details either as regards the powers of the advisors or
                    the individuals concerned.</p>
                <p>The question of possible representations by the President to the Shah is under
                    consideration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
